  "answer": "**Banana Bread Recipe**\n\n*Serves about 8 slices*\n\n**Ingredients**\n\n| Ingredient          | Amount                          |\n|---------------------|---------------------------------|\n| Ripe bananas        | 3 (about 1\u00bd cups mashed)        |\n| All\u2011purpose flour   | 2\u202f\u00bc cups (\u2248\u202f280\u202fg)              |\n| Granulated sugar    | \u00be cup (\u2248\u202f150\u202fg)                  |\n| Brown sugar         | \u00bc cup (\u2248\u202f50\u202fg)                   |\n| Baking soda         | 1 tsp                           |\n| Salt                | \u00bd tsp                           |\n| Ground cinnamon     | \u00bd tsp (optional)                |\n| Unsalted butter     | \u00bd cup (1\u202fstick, melted)         |\n| Vegetable oil       | \u00bc cup (or \u00bd cup melted butter)  |\n| Vanilla extract     | 1 tsp                           |\n| Eggs                | 2 large (room temp)             |\n| Milk                | \u00bc cup (optional, for moistness) |\n| Chocolate chips     | \u00bd cup (optional)                |\n| Walnuts / pecans    | \u00bd cup, chopped (optional)       |\n\n**Instructions**\n\n1. **Preheat** oven to 350\u202f\u00b0F (175\u202f\u00b0C). Grease a 9\u202f\u00d7\u202f5\u2011inch loaf pan or line with parchment paper.\n2. **Mash** the bananas in a large bowl until smooth, leaving a few small lumps for texture.\n3. **Whisk** together flour, baking soda, salt, cinnamon, and sugars. Stir until just combined.\n4. **Add** the melted butter, oil, vanilla, and eggs to the banana mixture. Mix until well blended.\n5. **Fold** the dry ingredients into the wet mixture. If the batter is thick, stir in a splash of milk until reaching a pourable consistency.\n6. **Stir in** chocolate chips and nuts, if using.\n7. **Pour** batter into the prepared loaf pan, smoothing the top.\n8. **Bake** for 50\u201360\u202fminutes, or until a toothpick inserted near the center comes out clean (occasionally with a few moist crumbs).  \n   *If the top browns too quickly, tent with foil for the last 10\u201315\u202fminutes.*\n9. **Cool** in the pan for 10\u202fminutes, then transfer to a wire rack to cool completely.\n10. **Slice** and serve. Store leftovers in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 4\u202fdays, or refrigerate for longer shelf life.\n\nEnjoy your homemade banana bread!\n\n_(This answer could not be fully verified \u2014 treat it with care.)_",
